            <ArticleTitle>[Pain in the foot or calf in a patient with varicose veins is not always of venous origin. Apropos of 13 cases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>261-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A leg pain is not always of venous origin. From thirteen clinical cases, various diagnoses are individualized: stress fractures, plantar static disorders, metatarsalgias, anterior and posterior muscular compartment syndromes.</AbstractText>
